    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Lachrimallion" hidden="false" id="6c2d-5f9b-da27-b658">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="9af8-288a-6ba2-141a" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Lachrimallion" id="75a7-8220-8a36-8226" hidden="false">
          <description>A model with this Order gains the Opus Viscera and Incorruptible Flesh special rules (Liber Mechanicum, page 99).</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Macroteknia" hidden="false" id="757c-56c8-5cd0-f00e">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="92a4-7e1c-9a1a-4529" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Macroteknia" id="78f9-4e6d-aa5a-6b14" hidden="false">
          <description>A model with this Order gains the Rector Aedificii (Liber Mechanicum, page 100) and Machinatus Primus special rules.
Machinatus Primus. Before deployment, select one vehicle without the Knight or Titan Sub-type from the same Detachment. If it is part of a squadron, only one model gains the bonus, and it must be clearly marked. That vehicle gains +2 Movement and +1 Hull Points.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Malaghrae" hidden="false" id="b193-34a2-bd5c-161c">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="133f-a4cc-8aa8-2b79" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Malaghrae" id="b490-513e-fe2d-fd7a" hidden="false">
          <description>A model with this Order gains the Mech-Assassin special rule.
Mech-Assassin. The model gains Preferred Enemy (Characters), Precision Strikes (6+) and Monster Hunter. Its Weapon Skill becomes 5 and its Attacks become 3, and it is equipped with a prehensile dataspike. It may exchange one power weapon for a paragon blade for +20 points.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Myrmidae" hidden="false" id="fe4a-cc1c-443c-0331">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="a813-5f99-d0d8-a267" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Myrmidae" id="df8d-fa85-2a17-69b3" hidden="false">
          <description>A model with this Order gains Hatred (Everything!), Bulky (3), Firing Protocols (3) and Precision Shots (6+), and its Wounds become 4.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Ruinor" hidden="false" id="a6ff-15c3-541b-4840">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="086a-3aa6-f2d7-7d47" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Order of Lesser Techno-Arcana: Ruinor" id="8d55-33ee-4844-944a" hidden="false">
          <description>A model with this Order gains Wrecker, Sunder and Secrets of Annihilation (Liber Mechanicum, page 101) and the Cybertheurgist Sub-type. Any unit it joins also gains Wrecker and Sunder while it remains in the unit.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
  </sharedSelectionEntries>
  <sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Warlord Traits" hidden="false" id="fd27-ce7a-55d0-205e">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="141f-5809-53f0-7ae6" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Warlord: Accursed Scrapcode" hidden="false" id="50d3-b04d-0eb2-e3c3">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="746e-6f92-7fbe-ec4d" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Warlord: Accursed Scrapcode" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="9388-f0b8-2e38-58be">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The controlling player may give the Corrupted Sub-type, at no points cost during list building, to up to three units from the Warlord's Detachment made up entirely of Infantry, Monstrous or Automata models. The army also gains two additional Reactions in the opponent's turn, usable in any combination of phases, while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="23e2-6bbc-4f60-9c96" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:"/>
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Warlord: Ever-Vigilant" hidden="false" id="6869-0c02-b559-6b77">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="9011-ff8a-abda-03ed" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Warlord: Ever-Vigilant" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="95c6-9f0b-2a20-9a27">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">When this Warlord, and any unit it has joined, Runs during the Movement phase, it adds the value of the Warlord’s Initiative Characteristic, increased by 1, to the distance moved, rather than the lowest Initiative Characteristic in the unit. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make an additional Reaction during their  opponent’s Movement phase as long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="94ac-3893-3712-42e4" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:"/>
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Warlord: The Logic of Victory" hidden="false" id="4442-442c-5445-0fa5">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="4d74-e288-5f3f-02ed" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Warlord: The Logic of Victory" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="0e70-dd85-712b-1953">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">If, at no point during this Warlord’s controlling player’s turn as the Active player, a Warlord with this Trait has neither made a Shooting Attack or been locked in combat then they gain an additional Reaction in each Phase of the following turn as the Reactive player. In addition, a Warlord with this Trait and any unit it has joined gains +1 WS and +1 BS when making attacks as part of any Reaction and +3 Initiative or +3 Movement when making a move as part of any Reaction.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="efdd-c854-96b0-c877" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:"/>
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Warlord: The Science of Slaughter" hidden="false" id="9a17-bbb8-bbd2-3816">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="583a-be40-884b-d485" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Warlord: The Science of Slaughter" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="5a67-e65b-3502-eb08">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">On the second turn of each combat a Warlord with this Trait is engaged in, and each turn it is locked in the same combat after that, it gains a bonus of +1 to its WS and +1 Strength (to a maximum of 10). Once a given combat has ended and the Warlord is no longer locked in combat, the Warlord’s WS and Strength Characteristics are reset to the original values. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make an additional Reaction during their opponent’s Assault phase as long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="faee-24b0-a786-c989" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:"/>
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Warlord Traits (Legiones Skitarii)" hidden="true" id="772a-068f-3f94-bc5b">
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="greaterThan" value="0" field="selections" scope="parent" childId="0176-56a3-d590-b103" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
        <modifier type="set" field="8c09-a3a7-cb0b-3b38" value="0">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="greaterThan" value="0" field="selections" scope="parent" childId="1ebb-8e01-7d58-9d99" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="8c09-a3a7-cb0b-3b38" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Encoded Hate" hidden="false" id="82de-ffff-c7a0-7653">
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Encoded Hate" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="b05c-fd6f-d6b5-37bf">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord and any unit it has joined gain Preferred Enemy and Counter-Attack (1). The army may make one additional Reaction in the opponent's Assault phase while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Full Frame Rebuild" hidden="false" id="616c-3496-d2fa-6128">
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Full Frame Rebuild" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="30e2-8187-9e90-a10e">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord has Eternal Warrior and It Will Not Die (6+). Its unit may not make Reactions in the Movement or Assault phases, but may make one additional Reaction in the opponent's Shooting phase. If the Warlord is removed as a casualty, the additional Reaction is lost and the unit may react normally from then on.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Uplink Override" hidden="false" id="58d8-9b44-c076-0c09">
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Uplink Override" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="d448-6b2a-a902-2932">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">While the Warlord is alive, all units in its Detachment with Datasphere Uplink gain Stubborn. The army may make one additional Reaction in either the opponent's Movement phase or their Shooting phase, not both, while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Open-Topped" id="2800-25c5-3c33-4bdd" hidden="false">
      <description>*Some hulls are open to the elements, letting their occupants fire at the cost of protection.* A unit embarked on a Transport with this special rule may fire up to five ranged weapons, measuring range from the vehicle's hull. If it does, it counts as having moved, which may stop some weapon types firing. Rules that let a unit count as stationary for shooting (such as Relentless) do not apply while it is embarked on this vehicle. Rolls on the Vehicle Damage table against a model with this special rule add +1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="0fc2-757c-fd37-2526" hidden="false">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <catalogueLinks>
    <catalogueLink id="5f24-4626-71c3-0547" name="Mech Library" targetId="3129-da35-55e0-642d" type="catalogue" importRootEntries="true"/>
